  "summary": "Mysore silk is variety of mulberry silk produced in the Indian district of Mysore, Karnataka.",
  "description": "Mysore silk is variety of mulberry silk produced in the Indian district of Mysore, Karnataka.\n\nKarnataka produces 9,000 metric tons of mulberry silk, accounting for nearly 45% of the country's total mulberry silk production. In Karnataka, silk is mainly produced in the Mysore district and is a patent registered product under Karnataka Silk Industries Corporation Limited (KSIC), a government of Karnataka Public Sector Undertaking.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Karnataka; registration 2004–05), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
